# BLoC Conventions

## 3-File Rule with `part`/`part of`

Every BLoC lives in `presentation/bloc/` as exactly 3 files. Events and states use
Dart's `part`/`part of` so they form one logical unit under the BLoC file:

```
auth_bloc.dart    ← declares the parts
auth_event.dart   ← part of auth_bloc.dart
auth_state.dart   ← part of auth_bloc.dart
```

```dart
// auth_bloc.dart
part 'auth_event.dart';
part 'auth_state.dart';

class AuthBloc extends Bloc<AuthEvent, AuthState> { ... }
```

```dart
// auth_event.dart
part of 'auth_bloc.dart';

sealed class AuthEvent {}
// event classes here...
```

```dart
// auth_state.dart
part of 'auth_bloc.dart';

sealed class AuthState {}
// state classes here...
```

> ⚠️ Part files cannot be imported directly. Always import `auth_bloc.dart` — it
> brings in events and states automatically.

## Events — Sealed + Prefixed

Events are named `<Feature><Action><Verb>`:

```dart
// ✅ CORRECT
sealed class AuthEvent {}
final class AuthLoginRequested  extends AuthEvent {
  final String email, password;
  const AuthLoginRequested({required this.email, required this.password});
}
final class AuthLogoutRequested extends AuthEvent {}
final class AuthStatusChecked   extends AuthEvent {}

// ❌ WRONG — no prefix, not sealed
abstract class AuthEvent {}
class LoginRequested extends AuthEvent {}
```

## States — Sealed

```dart
sealed class AuthState {}
class AuthInitial         extends AuthState {}
class AuthLoading         extends AuthState {}
class AuthAuthenticated   extends AuthState {
  final User user;
  const AuthAuthenticated(this.user);
}
class AuthUnauthenticated extends AuthState {}
class AuthError           extends AuthState {
  final String message;
  const AuthError(this.message);
}
```

## BLoC Handler Pattern

Event handlers are **always extracted into separate private methods**. Never write logic inline inside `on<>()`.

Naming convention: `_on<EventName>` — exactly mirrors the event class name with a `_on` prefix.

```dart
// ✅ CORRECT — register with method reference
class AuthBloc extends Bloc<AuthEvent, AuthState> {
  AuthBloc({required this.loginUseCase, required this.logoutUseCase})
      : super(AuthInitial()) {
    on<AuthLoginRequested>(_onAuthLoginRequested);
    on<AuthLogoutRequested>(_onAuthLogoutRequested);
    on<AuthStatusChecked>(_onAuthStatusChecked);
  }

  Future<void> _onAuthLoginRequested(
    AuthLoginRequested event,
    Emitter<AuthState> emit,
  ) async {
    emit(AuthLoading());
    final response = await loginUseCase(
      LoginParams(email: event.email, password: event.password),
    );
    switch (response) {
      case ApiSuccess(:final data): emit(AuthAuthenticated(data));
      case ApiError(:final message): emit(AuthError(message));
    }
  }

  Future<void> _onAuthLogoutRequested(
    AuthLogoutRequested event,
    Emitter<AuthState> emit,
  ) async { ... }

  Future<void> _onAuthStatusChecked(
    AuthStatusChecked event,
    Emitter<AuthState> emit,
  ) async { ... }
}

// ❌ WRONG — inline logic directly in on<>()
on<AuthLoginRequested>((event, emit) async {
  emit(AuthLoading());
  // ...
});
```

## UI — Use switch for exhaustive state handling

```dart
// ✅ switch forces all states to be handled
switch (state) {
  case AuthInitial():              return const SplashView();
  case AuthLoading():              return const LoadingSpinner();
  case AuthAuthenticated(:final user): return HomeView(user: user);
  case AuthUnauthenticated():      return const LoginPage();
  case AuthError(:final message):  return ErrorView(message: message);
}
```

## DI Registration

```dart
// ✅ BLoC = registerFactory (fresh instance per navigation)
sl.registerFactory(() => AuthBloc(loginUseCase: sl(), logoutUseCase: sl()));

// ❌ NEVER registerSingleton or registerLazySingleton for BLoC
```
